      "strengths_deep_dive": [
        "GiveDirectly's operational model is built on radical transparency and efficiency. In FY2024, they achieved a <cite id=\"4\">program expense ratio of 91.8%</cite>, which is significantly higher than many traditional aid organizations. Their fundraising is equally lean, requiring only <cite id=\"10\">$0.04 per $1 raised</cite>. This efficiency is paired with a <cite id=\"12\">working capital ratio of 11.4 months</cite>, ensuring the organization remains stable even during funding fluctuations. Their commitment to data is evidenced by <cite id=\"13\">tracking outcome metrics</cite> and maintaining a <cite id=\"7\">Platinum Seal from Candid</cite>."
      ],
      "summary": "GiveDirectly is a humanitarian organization that provides unconditional cash transfers to individuals living in extreme poverty. Since its <cite id=\"1\">founding in 2009</cite>, the charity has focused on the simple but powerful idea that people in poverty know best what they need. In FY2024, the organization reported <cite id=\"2\">total revenue of $140,343,295</cite> to support its global operations. The charity maintains a <cite id=\"3\">94/100 overall score from Charity Navigator</cite>, reflecting high standards of accountability. Their model is highly efficient, with a <cite id=\"4\">program expense ratio of 91.8%</cite> in FY2024. This means the vast majority of funds go directly to recipients rather than administrative costs. The organization has <cite id=\"5\">delivered over $126 million in cash</cite> to recipients in a single year. They operate in several countries including <cite id=\"6\">Kenya, Rwanda, Liberia, and Malawi</cite>. This distinction is important for donors seeking to fulfill specific religious obligations. The charity holds a <cite id=\"7\">Platinum Seal of Transparency from Candid</cite>, the highest level available. Their work is backed by a <cite id=\"8\">documented theory of change</cite> that views cash as a benchmark for aid. By providing direct assistance, they empower <cite id=\"9\">over 2 million beneficiaries</cite> to improve their own lives.",
